{% comment %}
  Secondary labels are gray only on the 2-bit and 4-bit palettes, the ones
  with real gray ink. Elsewhere they stay black: a 1-bit screen dithers gray
  text into speckle (TRMNL's reviewers flag it), and so does every colour
  palette, which has no gray and no prefix to override it with.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  Reusable blocks for the four layouts. The payload is built by
  apps/web/src/lib/trmnl/payload.ts and is fully formatted there:
  times are already in the owner's zone and language, so nothing here does
  date arithmetic. Liquid computing "time until" would freeze whenever the
  payload is unchanged, because TRMNL skips the redraw.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  `w--full`: TRMNL's value fitting shrinks the value to its parent's width,
  and in a centred flex column that parent is otherwise exactly as wide as the
  text, so a long winner's name never shrank.
{% endcomment %}
{% template lead %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--xsmall w--full">
  <span class="title lg:title--large">{{ lead.label }}</span>
  <span class="value {{ size }}" data-value-fit="true">{{ lead.value }}</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  Flag, race name, circuit, then round and dates. The full layout can combine
  the circuit and round/date line; half screens put the flag beside the name
  and the details below. The flag is decoration: in grayscale Italy, Ireland
  and Mexico are the same three stripes, so it can never be the only thing that
  says which race this is.

  `name_size` is the race name's size, `detail_size` the circuit and round's,
  and `flag_size` sets the flag's height, matched to the text beside it on OG
  and X. Its width follows the flag's shape, capped for Qatar, whose file's
  viewBox is 75:18 and stretches to fit.
  Widths over 128px use the named scale (`lg:w--max-48` is 192px): the
  Framework only generates bracketed sizes up to `[128px]`, and a larger one
  silently does nothing, which squeezed every flag on the X into the OG's cap.
  `shrink-0` keeps the shape in a narrow column, where flex shrank the width
  and not the height.

  Nothing is clamped: an ellipsis cut the dates off. The dates never split
  ("1 – 3 May"): their spaces become non-breaking here, because the Framework's
  label is a flex container that swallowed the space before a nested no-wrap
  span, and it has no text no-wrap class.

  The circuit and round are black, not gray: on the X, gray small labels
  were too faint to read at arm's length, and size alone already sets them
  below the name.

  Two copies of the flag: the OG's is marked `image-dither`, so TRMNL dithers
  it to the OG's few inks; the X's is not, so the X prints it as flat grays
  from its sixteen instead of speckle. `lg:hidden` / `hidden lg:block` pick
  one per device. The frame is a black
  box with 2px of padding (`bg--black p--0.5`), so white fields (Japan,
  Monaco, Poland) keep an edge against the screen. It was an inline border,
  but TRMNL's rules forbid inline styles, and the Framework has no all-sides
  border class; 2px is its smallest padding step.
{% endcomment %}
{% template race_header %}
{% if inline_flag %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--none">
  <div class="flex flex--row flex--left flex--center-y gap--small">
    {% render "race_flag", race: race, flag_size: flag_size %}
    <span class="title {{ name_size }}">{{ race.name }}</span>
  </div>
  {% if split_dates %}
    <span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">{% if race.circuit %}{{ race.circuit }} · {% endif %}Round&nbsp;{{ race.round }}</span>
    <span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">{{ race.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" | replace: "–", "‑" | replace: "-", "‑" }}</span>
  {% else %}
    <span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">{% if race.circuit %}{{ race.circuit }} · {% endif %}Round&nbsp;{{ race.round }} · {{ race.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" | replace: "–", "‑" | replace: "-", "‑" }}</span>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="flex flex--row flex--left flex--center-y gap--medium">
  {% render "race_flag", race: race, flag_size: flag_size %}
  <div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--none">
    <span class="title {{ name_size }}">{{ race.name }}</span>
    {% if compact_details %}
      <span class="label {{ detail_size }}">{% if race.circuit %}{{ race.circuit }} · {% endif %}Round {{ race.round }} · {{ race.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" }}</span>
    {% else %}
      {% if race.circuit %}<span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">{{ race.circuit }}</span>{% endif %}
      <span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">Round {{ race.round }} · {{ race.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" }}</span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% template race_flag %}
{% if race.flag_url %}
<div class="bg--black p--0.5 shrink-0 flex">
  <img class="image image-dither lg:hidden shrink-0 w--auto {{ flag_size }}" src="{{ race.flag_url }}" alt="">
  <img class="image hidden lg:block shrink-0 w--auto {{ flag_size }}" src="{{ race.flag_url }}" alt="">
</div>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The weekend timeline. `name` picks the row label: "label" spells it out
  ("Free Practice 1", "Sprint Qualifying") where there is room, "short"
  ("FP1", "SQ") where there is not. `tail` shows the last `limit` rows so the
  narrow layouts keep qualifying and the race. Each row carries its forecast.
{% endcomment %}
{% template schedule %}
{% assign schedule_limit = limit | default: 99 %}
{% assign schedule_offset = 0 %}
{% if tail and schedule.size > schedule_limit %}
  {% assign schedule_offset = schedule.size | minus: schedule_limit %}
{% endif %}
<table class="table w--full {{ size }}">
  <tbody>
    {% for row in schedule limit: schedule_limit offset: schedule_offset %}
    <tr>
      <td><span class="title title--small lg:title--base">{{ row[name] }}</span></td>
      <td><span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ row.when }}</span></td>
      <td>
        {% if row.weather %}
        <span class="flex flex--row flex--left flex--center-y gap--xsmall">
          <img class="image w--[22px] h--[22px] lg:w--[32px] lg:h--[32px]" src="{{ row.weather.icon }}" alt="">
          <span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ row.weather.temp }}{% if row.weather.rain != "" %} {{ row.weather.rain }}{% endif %}</span>
        </span>
        {% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>
        {% if row.state == "done" %}
          <span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ row.top3 | join: " " }}</span>
        {% elsif row.next %}
          <span class="label label--small label--filled">Next</span>
        {% elsif row.state == "awaiting" %}
          <span class="label label--small 2bit:label--gray 4bit:label--gray">Awaiting result</span>
        {% endif %}
      </td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endtemplate %}


{% comment %}
  `headline_size` is always passed. It is not called `size`: liquidjs, which
  renders the /trmnl page, resolves a missing `size` to 0 where TRMNL's Ruby
  Liquid falls back to a default, so the page and the device disagreed.
{% endcomment %}
{% template news %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--xsmall {% if fill or news.size == 0 %}h--full{% endif %} {% if news.size == 0 %}flex--center{% elsif fill %}flex--left flex--center-y{% endif %}" data-overflow="true">
  {% if news.size == 0 %}<span class="label label--small lg:label--base">No news yet.</span>{% endif %}
  {% for item in news limit: limit %}
  <div class="item">
    <div class="meta"></div>
    <div class="content">
      <span class="title {{ headline_size }}" data-clamp="{{ clamp | default: 2 }}">{{ item.headline }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% unless forloop.last %}<div class="divider divider--h"></div>{% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  A session result, up to `limit` rows. `split` lays ten rows out as two
  columns of five, where one column of ten would not fit. Both are always
  passed.

  Split by hand, not by TRMNL's overflow engine (`data-overflow-max-cols` on
  one `.column`), which TRMNL's rules prefer. Tried on 23 September 2026: the
  engine fills the first column before starting the second, so ten rows came
  out 7 + 3 on the OG and 9 + 1 on the X, and on a portrait X it clipped the
  list after eight names. TRMNL's own guide warns the engine is unpredictable
  on e-ink.
{% endcomment %}
{% template result %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small">
  <span class="title title--small {% if compact %}lg:title--base{% else %}lg:title--large{% endif %}">{{ result.label }}</span>
  {% if split and result.rows.size > 5 %}
  <div class="columns">
    <div class="column">{% render "result_rows", rows: result.rows, limit: 5, offset: 0, compact: compact %}</div>
    <div class="column">{% render "result_rows", rows: result.rows, limit: 5, offset: 5, compact: compact %}</div>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  {% render "result_rows", rows: result.rows, limit: limit, offset: 0, compact: compact %}
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% template result_rows %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small">
  {% for row in rows limit: limit offset: offset %}
  <div class="item">
    <div class="meta"><span class="index">{{ row.pos }}</span></div>
    <div class="content">
      <span class="title title--small {% if compact %}lg:title--base{% else %}lg:title--large{% endif %}">{{ row.name }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% template grid %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small">
  <span class="title title--small lg:title--base">Starting grid</span>
  {% assign half = grid.size | plus: 1 | divided_by: 2 %}
  <div class="columns">
    <div class="column">{% render "grid_rows", rows: grid, limit: half, offset: 0 %}</div>
    <div class="column">{% render "grid_rows", rows: grid, limit: half, offset: half %}</div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  `lg:portrait:table--xsmall`: stacked under the timeline on a portrait X,
  eleven rows per column need the same compact height as the OG.
{% endcomment %}
{% template grid_rows %}
<table class="table table--xsmall lg:table--base lg:portrait:table--xsmall">
  <tbody>
    {% for row in rows limit: limit offset: offset %}
    <tr>
      <td><span class="label label--small">{{ row.pos }}</span></td>
      <td><span class="title title--small">{{ row.code }}</span></td>
      <td><span class="label label--small 2bit:label--gray 4bit:label--gray">{{ row.note }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The way from the screen to the site, the same on every layout. `url` is the
  race's, or the standings' in the off-season. The link is the short /t/ form
  and carries
  utm_source=trmnl, utm_medium=qr and the screen phase as utm_content, for
  PostHog. 2px modules at error-correction level M leave room for content
  in the smaller layouts.
{% endcomment %}
{% template qr %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--center">
  {{ url | qr_code: 2, "m" }}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The lead session's own forecast under the lead, worded as the race pages
  word it ("Partly cloudy · 27°C", "Rain · 23°C · 60%"). Every layout shows
  it: an icon and a temperature alone read as an orphan, and the timeline rows
  only carry the compact form.
{% endcomment %}
{% template lead_weather %}
{% if weather %}
<span class="flex flex--row flex--center flex--center-y gap--xsmall">
  <img class="image w--[24px] h--[24px] lg:w--[32px] lg:h--[32px]" src="{{ weather.icon }}" alt="">
  <span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ weather.text }}</span>
</span>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The off-season screen: the season just run. `standings.title` is "Formula 1
  2026 Standings" and `standings.detail` "After 23 rounds"; before the
  season ends (only the /trmnl page shows it then) they say so instead.
{% endcomment %}
{% template standings_header %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--none">
  <span class="title {{ title_size }}">{{ standings.title }}</span>
  <span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">{{ standings.detail }}</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}The champion, as the lead: "2026 champion", then the name.{% endcomment %}
{% template leader %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--xsmall w--full">
  <span class="title lg:title--large">{{ standings.leader_label }}</span>
  <span class="value {{ value_size }}" data-value-fit="true">{{ standings.drivers.first.name }}</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  One championship table, drivers or constructors: position, name, points.
  `label`, `limit`, `offset` and `size` are always passed. An empty label
  leaves the second driver column aligned below the shared heading.
{% endcomment %}
{% template standings_table %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--xsmall">
  {% if label != "" %}<span class="title title--small lg:title--base">{{ label }}</span>{% endif %}
  <table class="table {{ size }}">
    <tbody>
      {% for row in rows limit: limit offset: offset %}
      <tr>
        <td><span class="label label--small">{{ row.pos }}</span></td>
        <td><span class="title title--small">{{ row.name }}</span></td>
        <td><span class="label label--small">{{ row.points }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The icon is inline, as TRMNL's guide asks: a URL can fail to load when the
  screen is drawn. Captured inside the template because a rendered template
  cannot see variables from outside it.
{% endcomment %}
{% template title_bar %}
{%- capture icon -%}<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="24" height="24"><g fill="#000" transform="translate(16 16) skewX(-12) translate(-16 -16)"><rect x="5" y="13" width="6" height="12"/><rect x="14" y="7" width="6" height="18"/><rect x="23" y="16" width="6" height="9"/></g></svg>{%- endcapture -%}
<div class="title_bar">
  <img class="image image-stroke" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,{{ icon | base64_encode }}" alt="">
  <span class="title">GrandPrixPicks.com</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}
